WEBVTT

00:00:00.860 --> 00:00:03.750
What is this about, Kasumigaoka Utaha?

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:08.730
What is your "what is this about" about, Sawamura-san?

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:13.240
Why has the number of girls appearing
in the pool event increased from two to five?

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.470
You know, when we went location scouting earlier,

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:20.040
I came up with lots of new ideas.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.360
Making such drastic changes on a mere whim...

00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:27.040
Did you consider the workload of the artist who has to draw the pictures for the story?

00:00:27.370 --> 00:00:29.620
You're only starting to draw them now, aren't you?

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:33.930
Work on the art seems to be quite late anyway.

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:37.140
This destroys the image I had in my mind!

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:39.870
Because of you, it may get unnecessarily delayed!

00:00:39.870 --> 00:00:41.240
Don't worry.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:43.230
If you need help with imagination, take a look here.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:50.110
It explains in great detail what the blonde-haired heroine,
Kawamura Spider Kirari, looks like in her swimsuit.

00:00:50.110 --> 00:00:54.610
It has too many mistaken descriptions, such as
"skin-and-bones", "flat-chested", or "padded chest"!

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:55.880
Oh my,

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.590
these are nothing but fictitious characters I made up,

00:00:59.590 --> 00:01:01.850
so I don't think they can be "mistaken".

00:01:01.850 --> 00:01:05.010
The physique was decided together with the character design!

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.180
Take a look at Hibarigaoka Kaho here.

00:01:07.180 --> 00:01:09.900
Why are you changing her to be this slim-waisted?

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:14.510
She was supposed to be a sloppier type, with a more bulging belly and big butt!

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:19.690
I have no recollection of ever approving that design.

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:21.700
The designs are the responsibility of the artist!

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:24.480
I wouldn't let a mere writer interfere!

00:01:24.480 --> 00:01:27.950
It seems our circle activities today are going as usual.

00:01:27.950 --> 00:01:29.360
Well, yeah.

00:01:29.360 --> 00:01:29.760
Whine, whine, whine, whine!

00:01:29.760 --> 00:01:30.840
Kasumigaoka-senpai's scenario is progressing,

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:32.320
Murmur, murmur, murmur, murmur.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:33.000
Whine, whine, whine, whine!

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:33.920
and Eriri's drawings aren't that late.

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.610
Murmur, murmur, murmur, murmur.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:38.360
All things appear to be going okay for now.

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:41.330
Yeah, it certainly is okay.

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:45.000
Your courage to say so certainly that everything is okay while seeing that happen, that is.

00:01:45.830 --> 00:01:47.800
Still, you know, Katou...

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.500
What, Aki-kun?

00:01:49.500 --> 00:01:53.880
I wonder why the two of them are on such bad terms.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:59.630
When I first introduced them, it was like they already knew each other,

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:02.260
and they've been doing nothing but fighting ever since.

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:03.620
Hey, Aki-kun,

00:02:03.620 --> 00:02:07.970
sorry, but could you read this line out loud?

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:09.880
Let's see.

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:11.390
"Huh, what did you say?"

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.780
"Sorry, I didn't hear you."

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:15.180
Thank you,

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:18.530
hard-of-hearing, thick-headed,
insensitive Main Character-kun.

00:02:18.530 --> 00:02:19.610
Wait a moment!

00:02:19.610 --> 00:02:22.800
What was this supposed to mean?!

00:04:03.540 --> 00:04:05.690
They really have it here.

00:04:06.540 --> 00:04:09.470
Sheesh, Tomoya-kun...

00:04:16.420 --> 00:04:17.230
Oh?

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.490
Hm?

00:04:34.430 --> 00:04:36.180
<i>Why her?</i>

00:04:39.460 --> 00:04:41.930
You're Kasumigaoka Utaha, right?

00:04:55.490 --> 00:04:59.270
Sawamura Spencer Eriri-san?

00:04:59.270 --> 00:05:02.290
Huh, you know my name?

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:04.960
Should I say I'm honoured,

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:07.260
snow woman with long, black hair,

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:10.260
no, Kasumigaoka Utaha-senpai?

00:05:10.260 --> 00:05:15.110
Unfortunately I'm not particular to being addressed with such an otaku-like nickname.

00:05:15.110 --> 00:05:16.420
If that's the case,

00:05:16.970 --> 00:05:22.160
isn't it all kinds of problematic to get so closely involved with a boring otaku underclassman?

00:05:22.160 --> 00:05:24.480
I saw you earlier.

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:26.550
You were talking with Tomoy-

00:05:26.550 --> 00:05:30.560
...with the first-year Aki-kun on the rooftop, very intently.

00:05:30.560 --> 00:05:32.610
You must have been mistaken.

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:35.810
That's Metronome of Love, right?

00:05:37.460 --> 00:05:40.540
You were talking about that on the rooftop, weren't you?

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:41.570
Well?

00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:44.580
Do you still insist I was mistaken?

00:05:44.580 --> 00:05:45.820
What is it?

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:51.100
Y-You two are actually otaku friends, aren't you?

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:52.260
That was unexpected.

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:55.200
To think that <i>the</i> Kasumigaoka Utaha reads light novels.

00:05:55.550 --> 00:05:59.120
But at least give up on that idiot.

00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.410
He'll just lower your reputation rather than be of any use-

00:06:02.410 --> 00:06:07.140
I'm used to being badmouthed, so I don't care.

00:06:07.140 --> 00:06:11.300
But if you want to use me as a reason to look down on him,

00:06:11.300 --> 00:06:13.180
I won't allow it.

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:16.080
What are you saying?!

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:17.690
Do you like him?

00:06:17.690 --> 00:06:20.720
I have no obligation to answer that.

00:06:20.720 --> 00:06:21.560
Tomoya...

00:06:22.540 --> 00:06:24.650
...doesn't love you in the slightest.

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:29.610
For him you're nothing but a friend with whom he can talk about the same book.

00:06:30.110 --> 00:06:33.780
He only loves Metronome of Love,

00:06:33.780 --> 00:06:35.670
its characters,

00:06:35.670 --> 00:06:37.330
and its author.

00:06:42.910 --> 00:06:46.880
Come to think of it, I didn't introduce myself yet, Sawamura-san.

00:06:46.880 --> 00:06:47.720
Huh?

00:06:48.020 --> 00:06:51.320
I'm Kasumigaoka Utaha from class 2-D.

00:06:51.320 --> 00:06:53.710
I go by the pen name Kasumi Utako.

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:55.700
H-Huh?

00:06:55.700 --> 00:06:59.930
I'm the author of his beloved Metronome of Love.

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:01.850
Nice to meet you.

00:07:01.850 --> 00:07:04.610
W-What?!

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:08.490
Why?! How?!

00:07:08.490 --> 00:07:12.250
Why is Kasumi Utako in our school?!

00:07:18.230 --> 00:07:20.790
I forgot to ask for her autograph.

00:07:25.440 --> 00:07:27.580
<i>This is currently my number one
recommended light novel of the year!</i>

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:29.280
<i>It's way above the "newcomer of the year" level!</i>

00:07:29.280 --> 00:07:30.660
<i>When you've read it, tell me what you think!</i>

00:07:30.660 --> 00:07:31.760
<i>Tomoya.</i>

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:33.860
I really can't!

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:36.870
I can't yield to that woman!

00:08:45.250 --> 00:08:47.280
W-Why do you ask about Eriri-

00:08:47.280 --> 00:08:49.080
Sheesh, you're hopeless.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:51.460
...about Sawamura?

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:52.630
No reason.

00:08:52.630 --> 00:08:55.760
She's just the most famous first-year student.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:58.300
I was wondering if you know her also.

00:08:58.300 --> 00:09:01.390
Well, I'm not really interested.

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:02.990
She's not in my class,

00:09:02.990 --> 00:09:04.170
she doesn't share my hobbies,

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:06.020
and her background is different.

00:09:06.020 --> 00:09:10.970
I am interested in Sawamura Spencer Eriri-san.

00:09:10.970 --> 00:09:14.030
I understand it's rumoured that she's half English.

00:09:14.030 --> 00:09:15.240
That's right.

00:09:15.240 --> 00:09:17.620
Spencer is her father's last name,

00:09:17.620 --> 00:09:19.750
and Sawamura from her mother.

00:09:19.750 --> 00:09:22.820
Her father works for the British embassy.

00:09:22.820 --> 00:09:25.290
He met her mother after moving to work in Japan.

00:09:25.660 --> 00:09:27.710
I wonder what she's like.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:31.300
From what I've heard, there aren't any bad rumours about her.

00:09:31.720 --> 00:09:36.050
Even though she's a rich girl, she's sociable, and nice to everybody.

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:38.800
That's just her faking it.

00:09:38.800 --> 00:09:43.430
In reality she's super egotistical, selfish and bad-natured.

00:09:46.710 --> 00:09:49.870
Tomoya-kun, do you speak with her often?

00:09:49.870 --> 00:09:51.700
No, not at all.

00:09:51.700 --> 00:09:53.230
I-I see.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:57.360
Because she doesn't speak to me at all in school.

00:09:57.360 --> 00:09:59.600
If she needs to, she usually just sends me an e-mail.

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.990
And even then, it's all nothing but requests.

00:10:03.010 --> 00:10:05.600
Just how long is she going to hold a grudge?

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:12.300
Um, Utaha-senpai?

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.000
What, Tomoya-kun?

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:17.650
Did I say something to make you angry?

00:10:17.650 --> 00:10:20.720
I'm fine, nothing's really bothering me.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:22.270
That's not true, is it?!

00:10:22.270 --> 00:10:24.820
The same to you!

00:10:27.340 --> 00:10:29.850
Kasumigaoka-senpai?!

00:10:29.850 --> 00:10:32.820
U-Um, you're looking for Sawamura-san?

00:10:32.820 --> 00:10:33.450
Yes.

00:10:33.450 --> 00:10:35.140
It's important.

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:37.070
Could you, perhaps, get out of the way?

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:41.280
B-But this is like her private atelier...

00:10:41.280 --> 00:10:45.410
Even us art club members aren't allowed to enter...

00:10:45.410 --> 00:10:49.570
Maybe she's getting carried away precisely because you're giving her special treatment like that...

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:51.390
That blonde princess!

00:10:51.390 --> 00:10:52.810
O-Oh, no!

00:10:52.810 --> 00:10:56.800
Sawamura-san speaks normally even with us first-years...

00:10:56.800 --> 00:10:59.420
She's a first-year to begin with,

00:10:59.420 --> 00:11:02.180
so isn't that just normal?

00:11:03.960 --> 00:11:05.660
And as a first-year,

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:09.180
she should pay more respect to me, a second-year.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:10.640
W-Wait a moment!

00:11:10.640 --> 00:11:12.660
She's not here right now!

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:15.020
In that case, I'll wait until she gets back.

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:19.530
Please open the door!

00:11:19.530 --> 00:11:21.520
Sawamura-san aside,

00:11:21.520 --> 00:11:23.530
the teacher is going to get mad at me!

00:11:23.900 --> 00:11:26.610
Kasumigaoka-senpai!

00:11:48.610 --> 00:11:50.520
Ah, Sawamura-san!

00:11:50.520 --> 00:11:52.490
Morning, Sawamura-san!

00:11:52.490 --> 00:11:56.020
Morning, Ishimaki-san, Satomi-san!

00:11:56.020 --> 00:11:58.280
Morning, Sawamura-san.

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:01.000
Yes, morning-

00:12:02.150 --> 00:12:03.780
Bleh!

00:12:04.230 --> 00:12:05.400
Bleh?

00:12:05.400 --> 00:12:06.780
Sawamura-san?

00:12:08.100 --> 00:12:09.210
It's nothing.

00:12:09.210 --> 00:12:12.250
G-Good morning, Kasumigaoka-senpai.

00:12:12.250 --> 00:12:12.890
Is that...

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:13.650
...the second-year...

00:12:13.650 --> 00:12:15.310
...Kasumigaoka Utaha-senpai?

00:12:15.310 --> 00:12:16.930
Why is she talking with Sawamura-san?

00:12:16.930 --> 00:12:19.000
Sorry to bother you right before school,

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:22.950
but could we talk for a moment?

00:12:26.180 --> 00:12:29.580
Why did you bring me here?!

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:36.650
I let myself into your private atelier yesterday,

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:38.320
Kashiwagi Eri,

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:40.900
the representative of the doujin circle egoistic-lily,

00:12:41.400 --> 00:12:44.660
a popular illustrator who pulls in long lines at various events.

00:12:45.090 --> 00:12:48.990
As a side note, most of your work is 18+ for-men doujinshi.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:51.670
How did you find even that out?

00:12:51.670 --> 00:12:52.660
I looked into it,

00:12:52.990 --> 00:12:54.670
based on this signature.

00:13:05.670 --> 00:13:06.800
What do you want?

00:13:10.320 --> 00:13:11.310
Perhaps...

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:14.790
"If you don't want everybody to find out, you'll do whatever I tell you to",

00:13:14.790 --> 00:13:16.060
you'll threaten me...

00:13:16.060 --> 00:13:19.150
"Enter, my men", you'll call out,

00:13:19.150 --> 00:13:21.650
and a bunch of brawny men bust in through that door...

00:13:21.650 --> 00:13:22.340
What?

00:13:22.340 --> 00:13:24.900
I-I would resist fiercely,

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:27.210
but I'd be no match against male muscle!

00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:30.160
They'd just grin lasciviously...

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.750
I wouldn't do anything that would happen in your doujinshi.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.540
You wouldn't?

00:13:35.540 --> 00:13:39.990
You wouldn't say "She's such a lady" while licking your lips, or anything like that?

00:13:39.990 --> 00:13:42.540
If you want to do that, just draw it yourself,

00:13:42.540 --> 00:13:44.530
you disgraceful doujin author.

00:13:44.530 --> 00:13:48.170
So, why did you find out everything about my true identity?

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:50.330
Because...

00:13:55.550 --> 00:13:57.100
Why do you hide it?

00:13:57.530 --> 00:14:00.480
You're hiding the fact that you're a light novel author, aren't you?

00:14:00.800 --> 00:14:02.980
I'm not particularly hiding it.

00:14:02.980 --> 00:14:06.830
It's just that nobody is reckless enough to come talk to me.

00:14:06.830 --> 00:14:08.780
Except one, right?

00:14:10.020 --> 00:14:12.330
How long have you been drawing those kinds of pictures?

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:15.850
Since my second year of primary school, I guess.

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:18.740
You've been hiding it all that time?

00:14:18.740 --> 00:14:20.960
Discrimination against otaku has deep roots.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:24.670
Such old-fashioned views aren't that typical these days, are they?

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:27.070
Don't say it like you understand!

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:31.240
I was mocked every single day.

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.260
Even the teachers didn't understand me.

00:14:33.710 --> 00:14:36.560
I was torn apart from my only comrade.

00:14:38.930 --> 00:14:40.800
Is that "comrade"...

00:14:40.800 --> 00:14:42.400
I just...

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:49.400
I just wanted to talk about the anime
and games I love with the friend I love!

00:14:58.450 --> 00:15:03.630
That bitterness from your childhood is the motivation behind your work, right?

00:15:05.300 --> 00:15:09.410
You don't draw to make people happy.

00:15:09.410 --> 00:15:11.760
It's rather more like revenge.

00:15:11.760 --> 00:15:16.320
You say that, but you don't aim to make people happy either, do you?

00:15:17.640 --> 00:15:21.100
You're not interested in anybody else, are you?

00:15:21.100 --> 00:15:23.150
You look down on most people, don't you?

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:24.480
That's...

00:15:24.480 --> 00:15:28.240
Your writing doesn't move people because of empathy.

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:29.770
It's all calculated.

00:15:29.770 --> 00:15:33.990
You simply manipulate feelings through your technique, don't you?

00:15:34.420 --> 00:15:36.780
My motivation is revenge?

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:38.550
Maybe so.

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:41.720
But you don't even have a motivation, do you?

00:15:41.720 --> 00:15:43.790
That means you're worse than me!

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:46.500
I was tricked and hurt,

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:50.510
by a book written by such a heartless author.

00:15:51.660 --> 00:15:55.420
Is that your impression of Metronome of Love?

00:15:57.040 --> 00:15:58.810
You know, Sawamura-san.

00:15:58.810 --> 00:15:59.770
What now?

00:16:00.720 --> 00:16:06.110
Even if our works are born out of calculation and revenge,

00:16:08.860 --> 00:16:11.030
the one who is moved loses.

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:14.030
See? You really take your readers for fools!

00:16:14.360 --> 00:16:16.430
I don't mean it like that.

00:16:48.540 --> 00:16:50.120
Well, that's fine.

00:16:50.120 --> 00:16:52.910
I am honoured by your words of praise, Sawamura-san.

00:16:52.910 --> 00:16:54.240
I'm not praising you!

00:16:54.620 --> 00:17:00.040
But you said that I manipulate my readers through my technique, right?

00:17:00.040 --> 00:17:03.980
That's the highest praise an author can receive.

00:17:03.980 --> 00:17:04.870
Maybe.

00:17:05.470 --> 00:17:07.360
Hey, Sawamura-san, I-

00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:10.310
You're manipulating him like that too, aren't you?

00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:11.860
What do you mean?

00:17:11.860 --> 00:17:15.380
You're leading men on a leash with that technique of yours, aren't you?

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:21.540
Being told that by someone who tempts men with ero doesn't make me feel anything at all!

00:17:21.540 --> 00:17:23.520
Who are you to Tomoya?

00:17:23.520 --> 00:17:25.680
I should be asking that!

00:17:25.680 --> 00:17:28.290
Are you perhaps his childhood friend?

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:29.900
What if I am?

00:17:29.900 --> 00:17:33.400
T-The bonds between people
are not about time, you know!

00:17:33.400 --> 00:17:37.030
L-Love at first sight grows cold as quickly as it happens!

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:40.920
In anime and games, childhood friends by and large end up losing!

00:17:40.920 --> 00:17:44.490
There's only a handful of works with an older main heroine!

00:17:44.490 --> 00:17:48.650
Blonde foreigner heroines are minor characters who come in third or worse!

00:17:48.650 --> 00:17:52.240
Characters with long black hair are so gloomy
that they'll just make the main character unhappy!

00:17:52.240 --> 00:17:57.590
Aren't childhood friends the gloomiest characters,
and a burden for the main character more than anybody?

00:17:59.350 --> 00:18:00.970
Um,

00:18:00.970 --> 00:18:03.470
so, for the next thing, you both take it home with you for now,

00:18:03.470 --> 00:18:05.980
and think about it calmly.

00:18:05.980 --> 00:18:08.100
I agree for now.

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:10.020
I'll start with that.

00:18:10.020 --> 00:18:11.330
Being calm, that is.

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:12.240
All right!

00:18:12.240 --> 00:18:14.650
Since we've decided on our direction for now,

00:18:14.650 --> 00:18:16.490
this is it for today!

00:18:16.490 --> 00:18:17.990
...but before that!

00:18:18.430 --> 00:18:20.200
An autograph board?

00:18:20.200 --> 00:18:21.990
Sawamura-san's and mine?

00:18:21.990 --> 00:18:22.910
Yes!

00:18:22.910 --> 00:18:26.130
For the winter Comiket participation announcement, promotion of our game,

00:18:26.130 --> 00:18:28.020
and a sign of making up today, and such.

00:18:28.020 --> 00:18:29.250
And a bunch of other things too!

00:18:29.740 --> 00:18:31.280
Eriri's illustration goes in the middle,

00:18:31.280 --> 00:18:32.380
and her signature on the right.

00:18:32.380 --> 00:18:35.510
And Utaha-senpai, you sign on the left side.

00:18:35.510 --> 00:18:38.290
Ah, Meguri would be a good character for the illustration!

00:18:38.290 --> 00:18:40.460
What, I have to draw an illustration too?

00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:41.470
Ah, you see,

00:18:41.470 --> 00:18:44.160
it's also to promote the game...

00:18:44.160 --> 00:18:47.130
I thought we could have it on display in our winter Comiket space...

00:18:47.130 --> 00:18:50.810
So, where will you display it before winter Comiket?

00:18:50.810 --> 00:18:51.840
Ah, you know,

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:55.180
a place where it will best catch everybody's eye...

00:18:55.180 --> 00:18:58.030
That means your room, right?

00:18:58.030 --> 00:18:58.860
What's that?

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:01.370
The bottom line is, you want it for yourself?

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:08.190
Also, Kasumi Utako's and Kashiwagi Eri's autograph board
would probably earn some good money in an online auction...

00:19:08.190 --> 00:19:11.050
I'm sure some would calculate so.

00:19:11.050 --> 00:19:13.250
Disregarding my signature,

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:17.970
an autograph board with an unknown author's scribble wouldn't be worth much!

00:19:17.970 --> 00:19:23.320
My, would you look at what the so-called illustrator
who hasn't even published commercially is saying!

00:19:25.310 --> 00:19:26.260
That's not true!

00:19:26.260 --> 00:19:28.390
It's a treasure...

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:31.870
...I've wanted ever since I started this circle!

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:33.360
Think about it!

00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:35.770
Kashiwagi Eri's and Kasumi Utako's signatures!

00:19:36.320 --> 00:19:39.150
It's the greatest collaboration in history!

00:19:40.840 --> 00:19:45.160
The producer who orchestrated that collaboration shouldn't be saying that.

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:47.140
Eriri...

00:19:47.140 --> 00:19:50.540
You really are hopeless, Morals-kun.

00:20:04.600 --> 00:20:06.130
Hey, Eriri,

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:09.910
if you don't mind, could you draw one for me, too?

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:10.560
Huh?

00:20:11.340 --> 00:20:13.830
Kasumigaoka-senpai, you too, please.

00:20:13.830 --> 00:20:18.080
It's not just Aki-kun. I've been wanting one for a long time, too.

00:20:18.080 --> 00:20:19.600
Katou-san...

00:20:19.600 --> 00:20:24.570
If it's too much work for Eriri, just signatures without an illustration is enough.

00:20:24.570 --> 00:20:27.190
No, of course I will, Megumi!

00:20:28.660 --> 00:20:31.710
In that case, I'll go get another autograph board.

00:20:32.760 --> 00:20:34.960
U-Um, Katou-san,

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:37.570
I'm sorry, but...

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:41.480
Could you get two more autograph boards?

00:20:41.480 --> 00:20:42.720
Make it three.

00:20:55.340 --> 00:20:57.610
Sure, got it!

00:20:57.610 --> 00:20:59.260
I'm going, then!

00:22:42.880 --> 00:22:44.390
I'm off!
